<title>ITALY: Italy's IFI denies merger talk with IFIL.</title>
<headline>Italy's IFI denies merger talk with IFIL.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agnelli family holding company IFI on Tuesday denied market talk over a possible merger with the Agnelli industrial holding group IFIL.</p>
<p>&quot;IFI and IFIL communicate that there does not exist a plan of merger between the two groups,&quot; IFI said in a statement.  </p>
<p>IFI is controlled by the Agnelli family, while IFI in turn controls IFIL. Both IFI and IFIL have stakes in the industrial group Fiat.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
</text>
